---
title: Palak Paneer
source: https://www.indianhealthyrecipes.com/palak-paneer-recipe-easy-paneer-recipes-step-by-step-pics/
---

Rinse the @baby spinach{4%cups} well, then drain.

Heat @oil{1/2%tbsp} in a #pan{}. Saute the @Thai green chilies{2}(deseeded), @whole unsalted cashews{8-10} and baby spinach for ~{3-4%minutes} until the leaves are completely wilted.

Cool the spinach mixture completely, then blend with @water{1/4%cup} into a smooth puree.

Heat @butter{1%tbsp} and @oil{1/2%tbsp} in the same pan. Once melted, add @cinnamon{1%inch}, @green cardamoms{2}, @whole cloves{2} and @cumin seeds{1/8%tsp}. Once the spices sizzle, add @minced onion{3/4%cup} and fry until translucent.

Saute @minced ginger{1/2%tsp} and @minced garlic{3/4%tsp} for ~{1-2%minutes}.

Add @garam masala{3/4%tsp} and saute until fragrant.

Pour in @water{3/4%cup} and cover, cooking until the onions are completely soft with some water remaining in the pan.

Lower the heat, then add @kasuri methi{1/2%tsp} and the pureed spinach. Mix well and cook until it begins to bubble, about ~{2-3%minutes}. If the curry is too thick, add a few tablespoons of water.

Add @paneer{150%grams} and mix well. Once the paneer is warm, serve with naan, roti or basmati rice.
